  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @brief Correlation of Q31 sequences (fast version) for Cortex-M3 and Cortex-M4.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length 2 * max(src
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * @details
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * This function is optimized for speed at the expense of fixed-point precision and overflow protec
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * The result of each 1.31 x 1.31 multiplication is truncated to 2.30 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * These intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit register in 2.30 format.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * Finally, the accumulator is saturated and converted to a 1.31 result.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  *
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * The fast version has the same overflow behavior as the standard version but provides less precis
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signals must be scaled down.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * The input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * Scale down one of the inputs by 1/min(srcALen, srcBLen)to avoid overflows since a
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * maximum of min(srcALen, srcBLen) number of additions is carried internally.
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  * See <code>arm_correlate_q31()</code> for a slower implementation of this function which uses 64-
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q31.c ****  */
